1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,080
The lift doors open, and Aziz taps Confirm under his own data.

2
00:00:04,130 --> 00:00:09,504
His names, his date of birth, and parts of his document number and his personal identification number.

3
00:00:09,554 --> 00:00:15,456
A minute ago, MyID read all of it from state records, and now it sits in a database of the bank.

4
00:00:15,506 --> 00:00:19,328
Who can read it there?

5
00:00:19,378 --> 00:00:25,256
In the lift, MyID checked his face, and the platform exchanged the one-time code for the result.

6
00:00:25,306 --> 00:00:29,144
The platform now keeps that result as his verified identity.

7
00:00:29,194 --> 00:00:35,696
Three things guard it: what the record holds, who may open it, and the trace that each read leaves.

8
00:00:35,746 --> 00:00:37,568
First, what it holds.

9
00:00:37,618 --> 00:00:43,448
The verified identity is a protected class of data, with stricter rules than any other record.

10
00:00:43,498 --> 00:00:53,720
It holds his names, his date and place of birth, his personal identification number, gender, citizenship and nationality, his document data and his registered addresses.

11
00:00:53,770 --> 00:00:59,936
It also holds the phone number that MyID gave, and an identifier from MyID with its expiry date.

12
00:00:59,986 --> 00:01:04,184
Images from the camera stay only when the bank turns image storage on.

13
00:01:04,234 --> 00:01:06,320
Nothing else lives in this class.

14
00:01:06,370 --> 00:01:11,936
His phone number, his phone and his network address are personal data too, but other rules handle them.

15
00:01:11,986 --> 00:01:17,792
The record is encrypted, and only the Vault of the bank can open it, as Lesson 6 showed.

16
00:01:17,842 --> 00:01:24,344
No part of the system keeps a clear copy longer than one request, and the identity never goes to a log.

17
00:01:24,394 --> 00:01:26,216
Now, who may open it.

18
00:01:26,266 --> 00:01:30,968
Inside the gateway, only one closed part of the code may touch this record.

19
00:01:31,018 --> 00:01:34,376
Every other part must ask it, and name a purpose.

20
00:01:34,426 --> 00:01:40,496
By default, the answer has masked values: only a few characters of each value show.

21
00:01:40,546 --> 00:01:44,024
Full values leave only for a short list of purposes.

22
00:01:44,074 --> 00:01:45,896
Keeping a new MyID result.

23
00:01:45,946 --> 00:01:51,896
The confirmation screen that Aziz just saw, and only on the phone of the session that gave the result.

24
00:01:51,946 --> 00:01:55,208
The phone check, which compares his number with the number from MyID.

25
00:01:55,258 --> 00:01:58,280
And the deletion job, when the retention time ends.

26
00:01:58,330 --> 00:02:02,768
An operator who opens a case or a phone review sees masked values only.

27
00:02:02,818 --> 00:02:05,192
Now the other side: who never gets it.

28
00:02:05,242 --> 00:02:09,944
The mobile bank gets only an identity summary: his level and his display name.

29
00:02:09,994 --> 00:02:15,632
No personal identification number, no document number, no address and no image.

30
00:02:15,682 --> 00:02:20,984
The bank's antifraud system, the notifications and the audit trail never get it either.

31
00:02:21,034 --> 00:02:22,496
Last, the trace.

32
00:02:22,546 --> 00:02:26,552
Every release is an audit event, with the reader and the purpose.

33
00:02:26,602 --> 00:02:29,384
Suppose an operator opens a case about Aziz.

34
00:02:29,434 --> 00:02:36,512
She sees the first two and last two digits of his personal identification number, and the last four characters of his document.

35
00:02:36,562 --> 00:02:40,112
The audit trail records her, the purpose and the time.

36
00:02:40,162 --> 00:02:43,328
Encryption stops a person who steals a copy of the disk.

37
00:02:43,378 --> 00:02:49,280
The audit trail stops a person who already has access, because each read carries a name.

38
00:02:49,330 --> 00:02:53,024
So the bank can always tell Aziz who read his data, when, and why.

39
00:02:53,074 --> 00:02:54,896
Now a check for you.

40
00:02:54,946 --> 00:03:03,424
The mobile bank shows Aziz his name on the home screen: does the app also get his personal identification number?

41
00:03:03,474 --> 00:03:11,224
No: the app gets only the identity summary, his level and his display name, and the full number stays behind the one closed door.

42
00:03:11,274 --> 00:03:15,448
One protected class holds his verified identity, and nothing else.

43
00:03:15,498 --> 00:03:19,480
The keys of the bank lock it, and only one part of the gateway opens it.

44
00:03:19,530 --> 00:03:26,896
Reads are masked by default, full values go only to a short list of purposes, and every release leaves an audit event.

45
00:03:26,946 --> 00:03:31,456
One field in the record still waits for a check: the phone number from MyID.

46
00:03:31,506 --> 00:03:35,968
On his record, it is his old university number, not the number in his phone.

47
00:03:36,018 --> 00:03:40,312
Lesson 15 shows how the platform finds out who owns his number.
